WEBVTT

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:05.640
That's the music that 
accompanies Gion Matsuri.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.790
Those huge yamaboko floats 
parade down Kawaramachi.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.750
It's no wonder the whole 
place gets super packed.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:13.610
One day...

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.850
let's go see it together.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.040
When we do...

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.950
we have to hold hands tight, 
so we don't get separated.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.280
Liar.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.560
Kyoto...

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.870
It's so hot.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.920
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.880
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.880
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:35.170
<b>A Summer Night's Accompaniment</b>

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.380
Today's yoiyama, the day 
before the festival, huh?

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.120
Why are you being so deliberate about 
saying that? You want to go or something?

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:40.220
Well, it's been ten years since I've gone!

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.670
Itsuka-chan said she wanted 
to go, too. Didn't you?

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:43.680
Really?

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.590
Then let's go together!

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.270
Huh?

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:48.640
I'm not going.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.350
Yay! Yay!

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.190
Come now, hurry up and eat.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.390
I'm going now!

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:57.440
Okay! Be careful!

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.020
I'm going now!

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.770
Stay safe!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.950
<b>G
I
O
N
 
M
A
T
S
U
R
I</b>

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.310
<i>Now that I think about it...</i>

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:14.120
<i>I told </i>her<i> that we should go to this 
year's Gion together, too, didn't I?</i>

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.500
<b>To Kanoko
\h I'm sorry</b>

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:20.010
<b>Carrying on
 a thousand 
years of 
prayers</b>

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.510
<i>Let's go see it together.</i>

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.970
Then let's go together!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.480
<b>For Pedestrians and Cyclists</b>

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.820
<i>Papa?!</i>

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:43.390
Huh?

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.910
The person running over there...

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.200
Isn't that Itsuka-chan?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.080
You're right!

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:52.440
Itsuka-cha...

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.950
Huh?

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.420
<i>Papa?</i>

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:02.220
<i>But what if it isn't him?</i>

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.800
Young lady, this seat is open.
 You can sit here.

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:16.460
<i>When he gets off the bus, 
I'll get closer to him.</i>

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.980
<b>Only for the Summer
 Ankoro</b>

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.980
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:22.330
Coming!

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.530
Hello, this is Irino.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:28.080
<i>Sorry to bother you when you're busy.</i>

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.660
I'm a homeroom teacher at Kitayama 
Elementary School. My name is Takase.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:36.000
<i>This is regarding one of the students 
in my class, Yukihira Itsuka.</i>

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.330
She's gone?!

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:40.040
Shh! I haven't told mom and the others.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.210
S-Sorry.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:44.600
He said some of the other girls 
in her class saw her get on a bus.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.380
A bus?

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:49.140
Her teacher told me to ask everyone in the 
house if they know where she might go.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.050
And right now, you're asking me, right?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:51.680
That's right.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:57.860
Itsuka-chan's father is missing, isn't he?

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.760
Somewhere like Kyoto Station, with lots 
of people always going in and out...

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.280
She said he might drop 
by a place like that,

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.260
so she goes there sometimes to see.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:09.360
Maybe she's near the station again.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:14.200
No, her teacher said that she 
got on a bus headed for Ohara.

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:15.830
Ohara?

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.330
Itsuka-chan is—

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.320
Shh!

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.870
This is terrible.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:22.670
Nagomu-san is out right now looking,

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.480
but he said to keep it a secret 
from the master and the others.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.600
I just need to create an alibi, right?

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:29.760
What's that?

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.600
A long time ago, I learned hypnosis for fun.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.600
What?

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.460
Oh, master! Can I have a moment?

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:37.120
What is it?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.610
<i>Nagomu-san, hurry up and come back!</i>

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:43.980
<i>Itsuka...</i>

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:48.610
We're almost there.

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:56.120
Papa, I smell something good.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.120
<b>Mitarashi</b>

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.120
Oh, they're making mitarashi.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:00.380
Here.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:06.130
They say that the Shimogamo Shrine was 
the originator of mitarashi dango.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.020
The dango there always have the top 
one slightly separated, you see?

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:15.820
When an emperor a long time ago scooped up 
water from the purifying mitarashi pond,

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.850
he saw a single bubble rise to the surface,

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.780
followed by four more. Some say 
they're modeled after that.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.040
Really?

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.800
Others say they're meant to be dolls 
that guard against danger.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:29.360
Then we should eat these for your 
next concert, and it'll be a big success!

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:32.440
You mean, my next concert 
"will also be," right?

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:38.030
<i>Ohara. Ohara.</i>

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.590
<i>This is the last stop.</i>

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.350
Excuse me.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:52.220
Do you know where the man with 
the guitar got off the bus?

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.810
I'm not sure.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.570
But someone else on the bus might have seen.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:01.230
Everyone generally heads 
toward Sanzen-in Temple,

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.310
so you might want to try asking them.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.020
<b>Path to Sanzen-in
 approx. 600m (about 10 min. walk)</b>

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.020
<b>Path This Way</b>

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.940
Someone with a guitar?

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:17.340
No, I didn't see anyone like that.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.620
I'm sorry, I don't know.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.580
We came here by car, so...

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.010
Sorry.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.010
<b>Kajii
Sanzen-in
 Temple</b>

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.180
<i>Papa...</i>

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:37.740
<i>Maybe it wasn't him.</i>

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:43.430
<i>I ended up skipping school.</i>

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.500
<i>I'll go home. I have to 
go back and apologize.</i>

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.660
<i>Twenty yen...</i>

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:54.160
Hey, you.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:54.760
Huh?

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:56.580
Is something wrong?

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.720
Um, no... Nothing.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:07:59.640
Really?

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.600
I-I'm fine! I'm on my way home now.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.970
You're in some kind of trouble, aren't you?

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:15.640
Don't worry. I won't kidnap you or anything.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.520
I'm Matsukaze Kanoko.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.030
I'm here from Tokyo.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:28.320
I'm sorry to make you keep me company.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:29.210
Not at all...

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.950
Um, these are...

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:33.720
I'm stress eating!

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:37.370
Honestly... These are really good.

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:41.740
It's delicious!

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:43.230
Isn't it?

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:46.800
Still, it's really hot.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.960
Yukihira Itsuka-chan, was it?

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:49.550
Yes.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:51.770
Why did you come here?

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.760
Well...

00:08:56.900 --> 00:09:00.140
I got dumped, you see.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.640
There's this idiot who 
chose his family over me.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:08.060
Even though he said, "Let's go
 to Gion Matsuri together."

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:13.490
So, in order to forget and to shed 
my misfortune, I came to Kyoto.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:17.070
Then mitarashi dango might 
be the perfect thing!

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:21.330
<b>Famous Ohara
 Mitarashi Dango</b>

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:21.330
<b>Kokumitsu Syrup
 Warabi Mochi</b>

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:21.330
<b>Chilled Sweet
 Zenzai Soup</b>

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:21.330
<b>Cream Anmitsu</b>

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:21.330
<b>Cold Hiyashiame
 Ginger Drink</b>

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.330
Really? Dolls that guard against danger?

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.380
I had no idea mitarashi dango 
had that kind of history!

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:26.260
I'll eat them with gusto!

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.540
You know a lot about them, don't you?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:31.420
Y-Yes.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.910
The person who taught me about them...

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:35.720
abandoned me.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:36.680
Abandoned?!

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:40.500
Sometimes I think it'd be 
better to forget, but...

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:45.150
Actually, I came here because I thought 
I saw someone who looked like him.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.230
<i>Itsuka-chan is so noble!</i>

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:51.240
But even though I was chasing after him, 
I was an idiot and lost sight of him.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:54.170
What are you talking about? It's better
 that you couldn't find him!

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:56.120
You should just abandon him instead!

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:59.980
Itsuka-chan, you're still young, 
and I know there are better men out there!

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.370
Better men?

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:04.200
Well, now, we should shed 
our misfortune together!

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:05.690
Excuse me!

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:07.080
But I'm already full...

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.080
I'd like to order some more!

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:10.080
Yes, hello?

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.410
<i>A girl wearing our Takayama 
Elementary School uniform</i>

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:14.170
<i>was seen heading toward Sanzen-in.</i>

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:15.710
<i>A bus company let us know.</i>

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.800
Thank you, Sensei.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:20.170
My car is just over there.

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:22.540
Thank you. I'm sorry for the trouble.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:24.400
Not at all.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.600
After I drop you off, I wonder 
where I should go next.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.990
Aren't you going to go see him?

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:34.540
I don't want to!

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:38.240
If he finds out I'm in Kyoto, he'll think
 I'm still hung up on him, won't...

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.000
he?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:42.700
Huh?

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:43.950
Huh?

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:46.060
Why...

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:49.840
Nagomu!

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.380
Is it true that the band broke up?

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:54.880
Nagomu...

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.190
If you're going to cry 
that much, then go try to stop—

00:10:58.190 --> 00:10:59.450
Kanoko, I...

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:00.050
Yes?

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:02.720
I'm going home to make wagashi.

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:06.310
Huh?

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.580
There was a letter with 
the sweets they sent me.

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:14.330
It says my dad was hospitalized.

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.950
If my dad has collapsed...

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:21.110
No one will be able to eat 
our shop's sweets anymore!

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:23.530
I'm the only one who can carry on the shop.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:27.500
Kanoko! Come with me to my parents...

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:29.370
Huh?

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:34.810
I'm sorry.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:39.010
I like Western sweets.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:40.220
Bye-bye.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:53.180
Thank you.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.440
I should be saying that.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:57.980
Thank you for keeping 
me company. Take care, okay?

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:04.660
When you're done, don't make any 
side trips. Go straight home, okay?

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:20.730
Itsuka-chan is a nice girl.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:24.840
Yeah, though she does 
have an impertinent side.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.550
Thank you for spending time with her.

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:28.970
She's about ten?

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.620
Well, she's in fifth grade.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:33.950
You came to Tokyo about 
ten years ago, didn't you?

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:35.400
Yes, I did, but why?!

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.840
You left without knowing a woman 
you'd broken up with was pregnant.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:39.710
Now, ten years later, you're 
back to meet your daughter.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.640
Is that the pattern I'm seeing?!

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:43.150
I think there's been a huge misunderstanding!

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.840
What misunderstanding?!

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:47.230
You're stretching out my clothes!

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:49.650
Her father's gone missing?

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:52.000
Huh? Then...

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.740
I was abandoned.

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:55.930
...was she talking about 
her father back there?

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:58.680
That's why my family's looking after her,

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:01.420
but my parents think of 
her like a grandkid.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.740
And she gets along great with everyone.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:07.530
She was cold toward you, though.

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:11.770
I'm trying to act like a 
father figure for her, but...

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.250
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.350
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:19.780
I see you're just as easygoing as always.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:25.240
<b>To Kanoko
\h I'm sorry</b>

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:26.140
<i>I thought he'd be hopeless without me, but...</i>

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:30.160
You seem to be doing well. How's work?

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.740
I quit. I'm job-hunting right now.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:33.300
I see.

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:38.250
But... why are you in Kyoto?

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:42.000
"Why"?

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:48.640
When I hear those sounds, it makes 
me really feel like it's summer.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.600
Gion Matsuri?

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.300
I'd like to go.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:56.640
<b>GION MATSURI YOIYAMA</b>

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:55.790
Then... should we go next year?

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:56.640
Huh?

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:58.900
I'll take you.

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:02.330
Okay!

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:08.750
No reason. Just felt like it, is all.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.480
I wasn't thinking about seeing 
you or anything, Nagomu.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.110
Yeah, I suppose not.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:17.790
Well, I'm going to go.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:21.110
Sure. I'll just get out here, then.

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:34.600
<i>What was that?</i>

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:36.180
<i>Being so nonchalant...</i>

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:51.190
Would you... like to get some tea or something?

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.580
<b>Kitayama
 Elementary
School</b>

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:56.370
I'm so glad. I was worried, you know?

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.890
Did you come alone? Where's your uncle?

00:14:58.890 --> 00:14:59.830
Huh?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.040
He was desperately searching 
for you, Yukihira.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:05.300
Make sure you express your gratitude to him.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.300
How far are we going for tea?

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.370
It's just over there. Not far.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:16.100
See? There.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:17.900
That's my place.

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:19.020
What?

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.480
Wait, Nagomu!

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:21.280
I'm back.

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.830
Just a moment please!

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.520
Allow me to show you to your seats.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.550
Shall I wrap that for you?

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.850
Uh-oh. This is a busy time.

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.740
I'm so sorry to keep you waiting.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.490
Wha—

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.750
It's you, Nagomu?!

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:35.870
What have you been doing?!

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.030
Don't just stand there! Go get changed!

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:38.910
I will.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:40.860
Sorry, Kanoko!

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:42.920
They'll show you to a seat 
as soon as one opens up!

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:44.120
Just wait there!

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:54.300
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:56.340
This is a gift, isn't it?

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.720
<i>He really is working in a shop.</i>

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:01.480
<i>And he's good at it.</i>

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:02.330
Oops!

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.480
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.670
Could I get a receipt for claiming expenses?

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:11.030
Let's see... The addressee is... 
What kanji are used for that, again?

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.390
Oh, if you'll please wait a moment!

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:15.870
Um, it's...

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.870
What are you doing working so 
slowly when things are so busy?!

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.370
<b>Allow me to wrap it for you</b>

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.370
Wrapping should be done deftly!

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.830
<b>Please check that you've received the correct change</b>

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.830
Change should be presented politely 
in a way that's easy to double check!

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.330
<b>If you would, please</b>

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.610
If you ask them to write their names on a 
blank sheet of paper, you lose less time!

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:28.280
My, you're far more helpful than Nagomu is.

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:30.360
You must be tired, Nagomu's friend.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:32.090
I'm sorry! I just jumped in without thinking!

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:35.630
It's fine! But I do have a 
little favor to ask of you.

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:36.970
What? I, um...

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.510
Oh, a customer.

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:40.390
Welcome!

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.900
<i>I reacted without thinking!</i>

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:47.730
I'm back...

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:53.150
How dare you just come wandering 
back like this, you moron?!

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:54.190
Master, wait!

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:55.110
Let go, Saki!

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:59.580
Didn't he say something like that 
when I first came back here?

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:57.200
Let go right now!

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.120
Wait!

00:16:58.120 --> 00:16:59.390
Let go of me!

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:00.910
Do you see that?!

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.450
Are you all right, young master?

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.590
What is this? What's going on?

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:07.560
I wanted to buy some time for 
you to look for Itsuka-chan,

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:12.080
so I tried hypnotizing him to think 
that you were still in Tokyo.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:12.760
What?!

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:15.580
Even if you come back now, 
there's no place for you here!

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:15.180
I'll try undoing it again. Please stand back!

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.430
Hurry up and undo it.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:19.390
My, you were really so much help.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:20.760
Thank you.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.090
Things have calmed down a bit. 
Please have some tea and relax.

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:25.980
Thank you very much.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:27.900
I'm back!

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.240
Welcome home!

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:30.900
Huh?

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:33.200
This is Nagomu's friend.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:34.360
I, um...

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.980
Nice to meet you. My name is Kanoko.

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:37.740
Huh?

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:42.430
Nagomu seems to be keeping how
 you skipped school a secret.

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:45.470
So I'll pretend that this is 
the first time we've met, okay?

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:46.790
O-Okay.

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:51.040
Here, please have some if you'd like.

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:54.050
Oh, it's waka-ayu, 
a sweetfish-shaped wagashi, right?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.960
Itsuka-chan, do you want to eat some, too?

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:58.330
Go ahead. Have a nice chat.

00:17:58.330 --> 00:18:00.170
Sit! Sit!

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:01.360
All right.

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:03.680
Wow, they look delicious!

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:05.530
Thank you for the sweets!

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:13.670
What a gentle sweetness.

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:17.790
Up where I come from, waka-ayu has anko inside.

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:22.160
But in Kansai, particularly Kyoto, filling it
 with sweet gyuuhi mochi is standard.

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:25.870
They say the ones in Kyoto depict 
the sweetfish in the Kamo River,

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.390
but in other regions, they 
use different rivers.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:32.920
With so many interpretations, wagashi are
 really interesting, aren't they?

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:34.860
You sure know a lot.

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:38.200
I-It's not like I looked into wagashi

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.700
because I was thinking 
about Nagomu or anything!

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:44.810
It's ridiculous, isn't it?

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:47.510
Why am I here?

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.530
Masa-san!

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:53.440
Finally, on the thirtieth time!

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:57.050
What's this? You all look exhausted.

00:18:57.730 --> 00:18:59.450
Nagomu? A minute?

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:00.540
What is it?

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:02.910
It's about your friend.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.740
I have to thank her somehow...

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:07.080
But I don't know what would be good.

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:09.750
That's true.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:14.250
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:14.250
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:13.110
Thank you very much!

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:17.960
<i>I ended up staying until the shop closed.</i>

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:20.260
Kanoko-chan?

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:22.440
Oh, thank you for the treat.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.770
I should go soon.

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:25.420
Do you have plans after this?

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:27.390
No, nothing in particular.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:30.140
Wonderful! Then shall we get changed?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:30.940
What?

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:34.220
Itsuka! Itsuka, you come, too.

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:41.110
It's lovely! It's one of mine, 
but it suits you very well.

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:45.780
Um, this is...

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.570
And you look lovely, too, Itsuka.

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:52.620
I was hoping you'd wear a yukata, 
so I had one of ours altered.

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:54.580
There. All done.

00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:58.520
Now, go visit the Yoiyama festivities.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:03.380
Oh, all ready?

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:06.260
I see. He arranged all this, did he?

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:09.990
Itsuka-chan? What's wrong?

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:13.000
With Papa...

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:16.190
One day, let's go see it together.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:20.010
I made a promise to go with Papa, so...

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:22.040
I think I should...

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:25.770
You should just go again with your father.

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:26.450
What?

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:28.440
Go again... with papa?

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:29.290
That's right.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:33.480
Depending on the circumstances, you can 
interpret things all kinds of ways.

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:35.000
Just like with wagashi.

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:36.460
And as for today,

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:40.710
just think of it as a rehearsal 
for when the day finally comes.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:44.080
You can think of that guy as 
a stand-in for your father.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:47.100
Now... let's go.

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:55.500
There are so many people!

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:59.050
Right? This is yoiyama.

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:03.980
I managed to keep my promise.

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:05.660
You remembered?

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:07.030
Of course I did!

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:11.420
Though, you might feel conflicted being 
brought here by someone you dumped.

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:12.380
Dumped?

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:13.840
Who did what?

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.870
Playing innocent like that really hurts me.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:19.920
What?

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:21.550
Nothing.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.050
Hey! Let's go!

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:24.830
Hey...

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.000
Itsuka!

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:32.810
We'll get separated.

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.900
Here. Take my hand.

00:21:41.010 --> 00:21:42.570
Huh? What is it?

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:46.070
Th-Thank you for today...

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:47.720
Nagomu-san.

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:53.820
You're welcome.

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:33.970
What? You got a job over here?

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:37.310
<b>Specializing in Kyoto Tea</b>

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:37.310
Yes, at a shop called Kafuuen. 
It specializes in teas.

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:39.050
What are you thinking?

00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:41.400
I'm back!

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:42.650
Welcome back.

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:43.960
Huh? Kanoko-san?

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:47.690
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:48.860
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:44.760
Why?

00:23:44.760 --> 00:23:46.480
Well, the thing is...

00:23:46.480 --> 00:23:48.700
I've fallen in love with 
Kyoto in the summer, so...

00:23:49.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>"A Blue Wind Rustling Fresh Leaves / Beating the Summer Heat"</b>

00:23:50.410 --> 00:23:51.840
Nagomu!

00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:54.120
What have you done now?!

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:56.370
This is my son, Tadashi.

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:59.620
Apparently the girl in the photo was lovely.

00:23:59.620 --> 00:24:01.120
That girl is...

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:03.120
<b>piece</b>

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:03.120
<b>yen</b>

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:03.120
<b>yen</b>
